# README wording — YOURS. The scaffold creates this file once and never
# overwrites it.
#
# A slot set here words the generated README files over the same slot of
# main.kit.info, where apidef puts the spec's metadata. A slot left out keeps
# the spec's wording. Text edited into a generated README is lost on the next
# generate; text here is not.
#
# The slots are title, summary, website, tagline, about_md, homepage,
# docs_url, meta_source and entity_desc. Any other key fails the model build.

# The summary is the first sentence of the definition's own description. It
# also stands in for info.description on the documentation site, which is
# written in Redocly's Markdoc ({% admonition %}, {% connect-mcp /%}) and
# links pages of docs.wise.com by site-relative path, neither of which
# renders anywhere else. Entity descriptions follow Wise's operation
# summaries.
main: kit: text: {
  title: 'Wise Platform API'
  summary: "The Wise Platform API is a REST-based interface that enables programmatic access to Wise's payment infrastructure: quotes, recipients, transfers, balances, cards and the profiles that own them."
  website: 'https://wise.com'
  docs_url: 'https://docs.wise.com'
  about_md: `**Versions.** Wise versions the whole API by quarter, in the URL. This SDK is
generated from version \`2026Q4\`: Production is \`https://api.wise.com/2026Q4\`, the default,
and the Sandbox is \`https://api.wise-sandbox.com/2026Q4\`.

**Credentials.** Most calls take a bearer token, passed as the \`apikey\` option: a
personal API token (Wise.com > Settings > Connect and manage apps > API tokens), a user
access token, or a client-credentials token for a Wise Platform partner. A partner's client
ID and secret come from Wise when the partnership begins. Each operation's own
documentation says which tokens it accepts.

\`\`\`ts
import { WiseSDK } from '@voxgig-sdk/wise-sdk'

// The Sandbox. Without \`base\` the SDK calls Production.
const base = 'https://api.wise-sandbox.com/2026Q4'

// The currencies Wise supports. The live API answers this one without a token.
const open = new WiseSDK({ base })
const currencies = await open.Currency().list()
console.log(currencies.map((currency) => currency.data().code))

// Every other call sends the token as \`Authorization: Bearer <token>\`.
const client = new WiseSDK({ base, apikey: process.env.WISE_API_TOKEN ?? '' })
const profiles = await client.Profile().list()
for (const profile of profiles) {
  console.log(profile.data())
}
\`\`\`

**Scope.** Every one of the 229 operations in Wise's published definition is here. Where
one entity has several routes for the same operation, an action tells them apart, selected
with \`$action\` in the request data: a card PIN is \`$action: 'pin'\` on
\`CardSensitiveDetail\`, a one-time-token challenge is \`'sms'\`, \`'voice'\` or
\`'whatsapp'\`, and each sandbox \`Simulation\` is named for what it simulates, such as
\`'balance-topup'\`. Two signing schemes the definition declares, HMAC request signatures
and JOSE payload encryption, are not applied for you: the operations that need them say so
in Wise's documentation.

**No MCP server.** Wise runs its own hosted MCP server for its API, so this SDK does not
generate one. The SDKs and the CLI are all here.

**Not yet run with a token.** The only live calls so far are to \`Currency().list()\`, on
Production and the Sandbox, which the live API answers without a token. Every other
request was checked against a local server answering from the definition. Wise's
descriptions are written in Redocly's Markdoc, and one parameter description in the
generated documentation still shows an \`admonition\` tag as text.`
  entity_desc: {
    account_detail: 'Bank account details by id.'
    account_requirement: "The fields a recipient account needs, for a quote's route."
    activity: "A profile's activities."
    address: "A profile's address: create or update, list, or get one."
    address_requirement: 'The fields an address needs.'
    balance: 'A balance account: create, list, get or remove one, convert or move money between balances, and get total funds.'
    balance_statement: 'A balance statement.'
    bank_account_detail: 'Bank account details: create several, or create a payment return.'
    bank_account_details_order: 'An order for bank account details: create one, or list them.'
    batch_group: 'A batch group of transfers: create, get or update one, add a transfer, or fund it from a balance.'
    bulk_settlement: 'A settlement journal.'
    business_profile: 'A business profile: create or update one.'
    card: "A card: list a profile's cards, get one, update its status or permissions, or reset its PIN count."
    card_holder_limit: "A cardholder's spending limits."
    card_limit: "A card's spending limits."
    card_order: 'A card order: create one, list or get them, update its status, and check requirements, programs and addresses.'
    card_sensitive_detail: "A card's sensitive details and PIN, read or set with client-side encryption."
    card_transaction: 'A card transaction.'
    case: 'A support case.'
    claim_account: 'A claim account code.'
    comparison: 'A comparison of what providers charge for a transfer.'
    contact: 'A contact, created from an identifier.'
    currency: 'A currency Wise allows for transfers.'
    delivery_estimate: 'The delivery estimate for a transfer.'
    delivery_update: 'A simulated transfer delivery update (Sandbox).'
    digital_wallet: 'A card in a digital wallet: Apple Pay and Google Pay provisioning, and payment tokens.'
    direct_debit_account: 'A direct debit account.'
    director: "A business profile's directors."
    dispute: 'A card transaction dispute: submit, list, get or withdraw one, or upload a file for it.'
    dispute_reason: 'The reasons a dispute can give.'
    facetec: "Wise's FaceTec public key."
    file: 'A file for a case.'
    funding: 'The funding of a transfer.'
    gpi_tracking: 'A SWIFT gpi tracking lookup.'
    hold_limit_breach: 'A breach of a balance hold limit.'
    incoming_transfer: 'An incoming transfer.'
    jose: 'JOSE keys, and a playground for testing JWS and JWE signing and encryption.'
    kyc_review: 'A KYC review: create, list, get or update one, or submit a requirement.'
    link_request: 'An embedded-flow link request, for KYC, payment instruments, recipients or disputes.'
    message: 'A message on a case.'
    multi_currency_account: 'The multi-currency account: eligibility, and its available and payin currencies.'
    one_time_token: 'A strong customer authentication check: a device fingerprint, PIN or facemap.'
    ott: 'A one-time token: verify its SMS, voice or WhatsApp challenge, or get its status.'
    payin: 'A payin.'
    payin_deposit_detail: "The bank transfer details for paying in to a transfer."
    payment: "A transfer's completed payments."
    payment_initiation: 'A payment initiation.'
    payment_instrument: 'A payment instrument: create, get or confirm one, or list its payins.'
    payment_intent: 'A payment intent.'
    phone_number: "A user's phone number."
    production: "A card's production status."
    profile: 'A personal or business profile, the owner of balances, recipients and transfers.'
    quote: 'A quote for a transfer: its exchange rate and fees.'
    rate: 'Current and historical exchange rates.'
    recipient: 'A recipient account: create, list, get or deactivate one.'
    rule: 'An authorisation rule for card spend.'
    saml: 'SAML single sign-on.'
    sca_device_fingerprint: 'A device fingerprint, for strong customer authentication.'
    sca_facemap: 'A facemap, for strong customer authentication.'
    sca_otp: 'A one-time-password challenge by SMS, voice or WhatsApp, for strong customer authentication.'
    sca_session: 'A strong customer authentication session.'
    settlement_allocation: 'A settlement allocation request.'
    simulation: 'Sandbox simulations: transfers, cards, KYC reviews, top-ups and incoming payments.'
    spend_control: 'The authorisation rules applied to an application.'
    spend_limit: "A profile's spending limits."
    subscription: 'A webhook subscription, for an application or a profile.'
    test_notification: 'A test notification to an application webhook subscription.'
    third_party_transfer: 'A third party transfer.'
    three_d_secure: 'The result of a 3-D Secure challenge.'
    token: 'An OAuth token.'
    transfer: 'A transfer: create, list, get or cancel one, and its receipts and payout information.'
    transfer_requirement: 'The fields a transfer needs.'
    ubo: "A business profile's ultimate beneficial owners."
    user: 'A user: create one, check one exists, get one, or set its contact email.'
    verification: 'Verification evidence for a profile.'
  }
}
